{
  "artifact": "shared/wizard",
  "kind": "skill",
  "note": "Five requests about an interactive `depot init`: adding one to a CLI that has only flags, a new setting that is both a flag and a question, quitting part-way, a runner with no terminal, and a secret among the answers. Graded by running the project's own entry point on a simulated terminal and answering what it asks, or with no terminal (checks/cli.mjs, checks/cli/wizard.mjs, checks/cli/kit.mjs). The grader recognises a question by its words (name, currency, low or threshold, token, a yes/no), so R1 states the questions it wants; a setup that asks in other words, or with an arrow-key menu, is not graded fairly. The skill asks for approval of a design before it builds, and a run has nobody to give it: R1 says to build without checking, the others name a fix. The back, review-edit, Ctrl-C and one-code-path lines have no request. Not registered in results.md until its first run.",
  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "prompt": "New people never know which flags `depot init` needs. When someone runs it in a terminal with a flag missing, ask for what is missing: the store name, then the currency as a code such as EUR, then show what will be created and ask `Create it? [y/N]`. Build it now; you don't need to check the plan with me first.",
      "fixture": "fixtures/cli-depot",
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "init-asks",
          "kind": "script",
          "script": "checks/cli.mjs",
          "args": ["wizard", "init-asks"]
